{"author":{"id":"686d9350e5e426946f54ca7a73ceeef9fd8682b44ea6617ce58187e451c43768"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791024665,"nonce":"buY3mgt7qHMpc6nA7MiUeRLYLxU=","title":"A raised error deadlocks the next call on HashLink: the raise longjmps past held locks","message":"GpuTest, run natively, hangs after \"beginning a second pass raises\": the next renderEnd never returns.\n\nxgpu's backend raises while holding a lock (pass_begin, compute_begin and computing raise with the encoder's MutexGuard alive) and expects raise to return; Caribou's does. hl_xidl's host::raise called hl_throw, which longjmps back into HashLink without running Rust destructors, so the guard was never dropped and the encoder stayed locked.\n\nhl_xidl's raise now records the message and returns. x-idl's generated HashLink wrapper calls host::throw_pending once the call has returned, when nothing is held. Helpers that cannot continue after raising use host::fail, which records and unwinds to the wrapper's catch_unwind.\n\nAn adapter over hl_xidl must re-export host::throw_pending: hlwgpu's runtime does; hlwindow's does when it moves to an x-idl with the new wrapper.","files":null}]}